From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 08:34:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fonts: Report the load state of @font-face rules in
 FontFace.status

A FontFace for an @font-face rule was created with the status "loading"
and kept it forever, and its `loaded` promise never settled, so awaiting
`FontFace.load()` on such a face hung. Keep the load state on the rule,
which the FontContext and the FontFace share, and settle the promise when
the state changes. A rejection is marked handled, because the object exists
whether or not the page asked for the font.

Fork note: first of four patches that stop Servo from downloading every
@font-face rule; this one also stands on its own. Meant for upstream; the code is the same
as in the upstream-based version.

Relies on: `FontFaceRuleInfo` being shared between the FontContext and the
css-connected FontFace (upstream #45975/#46271), and on
`ScriptThread::handle_web_font_loaded` / `Document::maybe_fulfill_font_ready_promise`
as the places where a finished load reaches script.

Drop when upstream reports the load state of css-connected faces: on plain
upstream, `css/css-fonts/font-palette-add.html` then finishes instead of
timing out (it awaits `[...document.fonts][0].load()`), and a css-connected
face reports "loaded" once its font is in use.

Upstream's MathML tests, enabled in #49127, wait for `loadAllFonts()` of
mathml/support/fonts.js, which awaits `FontFace.load()` for every face
in `document.fonts`. On upstream that promise never settles for the face
of an @font-face rule, so 100 of the tests time out, and upstream
expects TIMEOUT. With this patch they finish: 92 expectations change,
and 8 go because the tests pass. Five tests end in ERROR because MathML
elements lack `dataset`, not in a crash. When upstream reports the load
state of css-connected faces, which is when this patch can be dropped,
upstream's expectations change the same way.

Validation: `./mach test-wpt --release --processes 1 css/css-font-loading css/css-fonts html/canvas/element/text html/canvas/offscreen/text` (947 tests): font-palette-{add,modify,remove}-2 now pass and font-palette-{add,modify,remove} fail on the unimplemented `font-palette` instead of timing out (expectations updated); the only other unexpected result, font-variant-emoji-1 FAIL, also happens on plain ohos-main. font-variant-emoji-2 and matching/font-unicode-presented-as-emoji-outline keep upstream's FAIL expectations: they fail whenever a colour emoji font is installed, as on CI, and pass only without one. 2026-11-09 sync: `./mach test-wpt --processes 8 --timeout-multiplier 2 mathml` with release builds (2026-10-29): on plain upstream the 100 tests time out as expected; with the stack up to this patch they finish with the same results as on the ohos-main tip, where SpiderMonkey and QuickJS give identical results, subtests included. This sync's full QuickJS run and its reruns with both engines have no unexpected MathML result but mo-single-char-and-children's, which fails on plain 0.8.0 too.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; written and tested by the agent, ported from upstream main to ohos-main's Rc<Promise> API)
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; 2026-10-08 sync -- conflict resolution for upstream's RootedPromise conversion (#47935, #48333), resolved to the code of the upstream-bound lazy-webfonts branch; folded the squash commit that keeps the two colour-emoji FAIL expectations)
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; 2026-11-09 sync -- folded in "fixup! fonts: Report the load state of @font-face rules in FontFace.status" (bisected and written by the agent between syncs): the expectations of upstream's MathML tests, which finish with this patch)
